From cca37e5ae87680beec23abef74507ca3a54ea568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] nvme: log the controller's state right after a start
 from off

A J604 Stage 2 parked after a start of ANS from off with CSTS reading the
controller fatal status (0x2) and CC.EN clear, read after the failure,
with BOOT_STATUS ok. Whether the fatal status was already there before
this stage wrote anything to the controller, or came with the enable,
decides where the fault is. Log RUN, CC, CSTS and BOOT_STATUS once the
firmware reports booted, before any write to CC.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/nvme.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvme.c b/src/nvme.c
index 162b73f3..e1c5bbdb 100644
--- a/src/nvme.c
+++ b/src/nvme.c
@@ -532,6 +532,8 @@ static bool nvme_ans_power_on(void)
         if (nvme_ans_start(try)) {
             nvme_boot_ticks = get_ticks();
             printf("nvme: ANS started from off%s\n", try ? " on a retry" : "");
+            /* Before any write to CC: whether the controller reports a fault already. */
+            nvme_ans_log_state("started from off");
             return true;
         }
     }
